.TH CLogMonitor.n n 03/08/98 "CADC"
.BS
.SH NAME
CLogMonitor 
\- Create and manipulate a widget which monitors a status record and 
   maintain a log of its value..

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBCLogMonitor\fI \fIpathName \fR?\fIoptions\fR?

.SH "INHERITANCE"
itk::Widget \<- iwidgets::Labeledwidget \<- iwidgets::Entryfield 
\<- iwidgets::Combobox \<- CLogMonitor

.SO
\-background	\-borderwidth	\-cursor	
\-exportselection	\-foreground	\-highlightcolor	
\-highlightthickness	\-insertbackground	\-insertborderwidth	
\-insertofftime	\-insertontime	\-insertwidth	
\-justify	\-relief	\-selectbackground
\-selectborderwidth	\-selectforeground	\-selectbackground
\-width
.SE


.SH "ASSOCIATED OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-hscrollmode\fR	\fB\-items\fR	\fB\-textbackground\fR
\fB\-textfont\fR	\fB\-vscrollmode\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBscrolledlistbox\fR manual entry for details on the above options.

.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-show\fR	\fB\-state\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBentry\fR manual entry for details on the above options.


.SH "INHERITED OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-cliendata\fR	\fB\-labelbitmap\fR	\fB\-labelfont\fR
\fB\-labelimage\fR	\fB\-labelmargin\fR	\fB\-lablepos\fR
\fB\-labeltext\fR	\fB\-labelvariable\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBiwidgets::Labeledwidget\fR class manual entry for descriptions 
for the above options.

.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-childsitepos\fR	\fB\-command\fR	\fB\-fixed\fR
\fB\-focuscommand\fR	\fB\-invalid\fR	\fB\-validate\fR
\fB\-textvariable\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBiwidgets::Entryfield\fR class manual entry for descriptions 
for the above options.

.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-arrowrelief\fR	\fB\-autoclear\fR	\fB\-dropdown\fR
\fB\-editable\fR	\fB\-fliparrow\fR	\fB\-listheight\fR
\fB\-margin\fR	\fB\-popupcursor\fR	\fB\-unique\fR
.fi
.LP
See the \fBiwdigets::Combobox\fR class manual entry for descriptions for the
above options.

.SH "WIDGET-SPECIFIC OPTIONS"

.OP \-length length Length
Specifies the log length, the number of values retained for the 
status record that is being monitored.
Default value is 50.	

.OP \-logcommand logCommand Command
Specifies a command that is executed whenever a the value of
the status record changes.  The "log" is appended to the command.

.BE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBCLogMonitor\fR command creates a new window (given by the
\fIpathName\fR argument) and makes it into a CLogMonitor widget.
Additional options, described above, may be specified on the 
command line or in the option database to configure aspects of
the LED. The \fBCLogMonitor\fR command returns its
\fIpathName\fR argument.  At the time this command is invoked,
there must not exist a window named \fIpathName\fR, but
\fIpathName\fR's parent must exist.

.SH "ASSOCIATED COMMANDS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fBicursor\fR	\fBscan\fR
.fi 
.LP
See the \fBentry\fR manual entry for details on the above commands.

.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fBcurselection\fR	\fBindex\fR	\fBsee\fR
\fBsize\fR	\fBxview\fR	\fByview\fR
.fi 
.LP
See the \fBlistbox\fR manual entry for details on the above commands.

.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fBgetcurselection\fR	\fBjustify\fR	\fBsort\fR
.fi 
.LP
See the \fBscrolledlistbox\fR manual entry for details on the above commands.


.SH "INHERITED COMMANDS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fBclear\fR	\fBdelete\fR	\fBget\fR	
\fBinsert\fR	\fBselection\fR
.fi 
.LP
See the \fBiwdigets::Combobox\fR class manual entry for details on the 
inherited commands

.SH "WIDGET COMMAND"
The \fBCLogMonitor\fR command creates a new Tcl command whose
name is \fIpathName\fR.  This
command may be used to invoke various
operations on the widget.  It has the following general form:
.CS
\fIpathName method \fR?\fIarg arg ...\fR?
.CE
\fImethod\fR and the \fIarg\fRs
determine the exact behavior of the command.  
.PP
The following methods are possible for CLogMonitor widgets:
.TP
\fIpathName \fBcget\fR \fIoption\fR
Returns the current value of the configuration option given
by \fIoption\fR.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCLogMonitor\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBchildsite\fR
Return the path name of the child site.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcomponent\fR ?\fIname\fR? ?\fIcommand arg arg ...\fR?
Used to query or access component widgets within the log monitor
widget.  With no arguments, this returns a list of
symbolic names for component widgets that are accessible in the
current scope.  
.sp
If a symbolic \fIname\fR is specified this method returns the window
path name for that component.
.sp
Otherwise, the \fIcommand\fR and any remaining \fIarg\fR arguments
are invoked as a method on the component with the symbolic \fIname\fR.
This provides a well-defined mechanism for accessing internal components
without relying on specific window path names.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBconfig\fR
See \fBconfigure\fI.

.TP
\fIpathName\fR \fBconfigure\fR ?\fIoption\fR? ?\fIvalue option value ...\fR?
Query or modify the configuration options of the widget.
If no \fIoption\fR is specified, returns a list describing all of
the available options for \fIpathName\fR (see \fBTk_ConfigureInfo\fR for
information on the format of this list).  If \fIoption\fR is specified
with no \fIvalue\fR, then the command returns a list describing the
one named option (this list will be identical to the corresponding
sublist of the value returned if no \fIoption\fR is specified).  If
one or more \fIoption\-value\fR pairs are specified, then the command
modifies the given widget option(s) to have the given value(s);  in
this case the command returns an empty string.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCLed\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBgetLog\fR
Returns the current log as a list.  Each status record value is an 
item in the list.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBisa\fR \fBclassName\fR
Sets the log monitor's class to the specified class name.

.SH "DEFAULT BINDINGS"
.PP
No bindings are defined for this widget except those defined for the
various components this widget is comprised of.
See the \fBcombobox\fR, \fBscrolledlistbox\fR, \fBlistbox\fR, 
\fBentry\fB, and \fBbutton\fR manual
pages for more information.

.SH EXAMPLE
.DS
 CDhgStatus dhsStatus "CMD DTS HIS QLS STA"
 CLogMonitor .log dhsStatus dhsLog
      -editable false                                         \ 
      -labeltext [ lindex $_dhgDefaults(dhs,statusDesc) $i ]  \ 
      -relief ridge                                           \ 
      -textfont $_dhgDefaults(entryFont)                      \ 
      -unique false 
 pack .log -fill x -padx 5 -pady5
.DE

.SH AUTHOR
Shannon Jaeger

.SH KEYWORDS
log, status record, monitor, widget
